========================================================================
(3) DEDEKIND SUMS of LRC bindings + RECIPROCITY as the sheaf gluing (CF descent)
========================================================================
   AP tight  (D=14,a=1):  s(1,14) = 13/14 = +0.9286;  reciprocity holds: True
   covering-min constr (D=Phi6=183,a=14):  s(14,183) = -91/1098 = -0.0829;  reciprocity holds: True
   (n+q)-witness q=13 (D=27,a=25):  s(25,27) = -143/162 = -0.8827;  reciprocity holds: True
   (n+q)-witness q=11 (D=25,a=16):  s(16,25) = -4/25 = -0.1600;  reciprocity holds: True
   covering-min beater n=10 (D=37,a=?):  s(10,37) = 3/37 = +0.0811;  reciprocity holds: True

   RECIPROCITY = the two-modulus GLUING: s(a,D) [modulus D] <-> s(D,a) [modulus a<D], the
   Euclidean/continued-fraction DESCENT. Iterating it walks D down its CF [n-1, a(n)] --
   the SAME Farey/three-gap ladder the covering-min lives on (HYP-3732/3762). The descent
   TERMINATES at small modulus (base case) UNLESS an obstruction (E2 anomaly / genus cusp
   form, HYP-3587) blocks it -- that obstruction IS the iota-odd degree residual.
